--- Plant Cable Runs & Trap Analysis ---
  (a) Robot cell near welders (85 m)  -> Cat6A S/FTP (shielded; <100 m limit; blocks arc-welding EMI)
  (b) Office to shop-floor (140 m)   -> Multimode Fibre OM3/OM4 (TRAP: 140 m > 100 m Cat6/Cat6A limit!)
  (c) Shop floor to DC (550 m)       -> Single-mode Fibre (OS2; 550 m exceeds 10G OM3/OM4 300-400 m limit)
  (d) Plant to head office (400 km)  -> Leased Line / Carrier MPLS over Single-mode Fibre

  250 MHz cable @ 40 dB SNR (clean)  : 3321.96 Mbps
  250 MHz cable @ 15 dB SNR (welders): 1256.95 Mbps (-62.2% capacity drop)
  Why real speed < Shannon limit     : Protocol headers, guard bands, attenuation, ISI, finite modulation/FEC.

--- Alternative Concept: Wi-Fi 6 (160 MHz, 15 dB SNR near welders) ---
  Shannon capacity @ 15 dB           : 804.45 Mbps (theoretical ceiling)
  Verdict: NOT acceptable for 10 ms robot commands — CSMA/CA contention + arc-welding EMI
           induce retries and non-deterministic latency > 10 ms.
